{"qid": 273, "answered": null, "resp": "Concept attainment involves identifying the essential features that define a category and distinguishing its members from nonmembers. Three common ways of attaining concepts are:\nFINAL: (1) **Direct experience and observation:** Learners interact with objects or situations and discover their shared characteristics\u2014for example, examining different plants to understand \u201cplant.\u201d (2) **Comparison of examples and nonexamples:** Learners identify defining features by contrasting instances that belong to a concept with those that do not\u2014for example, comparing triangles with other shapes. (3) **Definitions and explanations:** Learners acquire a concept through language or instruction, then clarify and apply it using examples\u2014for example, learning the definition of \u201cdemocracy\u201d and examining different political systems.", "final": "(1) **Direct experience and observation:** Learners interact with objects or situations and discover their shared characteristics\u2014for example, examining different plants to understand \u201cplant.\u201d (2) **Comparison of examples and nonexamples:** Learners identify defining features by contrasting instances that belong to a concept with those that do not\u2014for example, comparing triangles with other shapes. (3) **Definitions and explanations:** Learners acquire a concept through language or instruction, then clarify and apply it using examples\u2014for example, learning the definition of \u201cdemocracy\u201d and examining different political systems."}
