{"qid": 383, "answered": null, "resp": "Under the Age Discrimination in Employment Act, replacing a qualified employee aged 40 or older with a substantially younger worker can support an inference of age discrimination. The replacement need not be under 40, and this evidence alone does not conclusively establish discrimination.\nFINAL: When a qualified employee aged 40 or older is fired and replaced by a substantially younger worker, even if the replacement is also over 40.", "final": "When a qualified employee aged 40 or older is fired and replaced by a substantially younger worker, even if the replacement is also over 40."}
