{"qid": 408, "answered": null, "resp": "Carl Rogers viewed personality through a humanistic lens: people have an innate drive toward growth and self-actualization, supported by unconditional positive regard. Psychological well-being depends on congruence between one\u2019s self-concept and lived experience.\nFINAL: Personality develops through an innate drive toward self-actualization, with healthy growth fostered by unconditional positive regard and a congruent self-concept.", "final": "Personality develops through an innate drive toward self-actualization, with healthy growth fostered by unconditional positive regard and a congruent self-concept."}
