{"qid": 425, "answered": null, "resp": "Ethical guidelines allow psychologists to provide emergency services outside their usual competence when more appropriate services are unavailable, so that urgently needed care is not denied. Assess the girl\u2019s immediate safety and needs, provide crisis support, and seek consultation while arranging appropriate follow-up care.\nFINAL: Provide emergency crisis intervention despite your limited experience, seek consultation, and discontinue or transfer those emergency services when the crisis ends or appropriate services become available.", "final": "Provide emergency crisis intervention despite your limited experience, seek consultation, and discontinue or transfer those emergency services when the crisis ends or appropriate services become available."}
