{"qid": 431, "answered": null, "resp": "Catharsis theory proposes that expressing aggression releases pent-up frustration and aggressive energy, reducing the likelihood of further aggression. Research does not support this claim; venting aggression can instead reinforce or increase it.\nFINAL: Expressing aggression supposedly \u201cvents\u201d frustration and reduces subsequent aggression, but research does not support this catharsis effect.", "final": "Expressing aggression supposedly \u201cvents\u201d frustration and reduces subsequent aggression, but research does not support this catharsis effect."}
