{"qid": 461, "answered": null, "resp": "FINAL: Stern\u2019s (1956) **theory of convergence** holds that development results from the interaction of heredity (nature) and environment (nurture). Inherited dispositions provide potentials, while environmental conditions influence how they are expressed; neither factor alone adequately explains development.", "final": "Stern\u2019s (1956) **theory of convergence** holds that development results from the interaction of heredity (nature) and environment (nurture). Inherited dispositions provide potentials, while environmental conditions influence how they are expressed; neither factor alone adequately explains development."}
{"qid": 462, "answered": null, "resp": "FINAL: Meditation can reduce sympathetic (\u201cfight-or-flight\u201d) activity and promote parasympathetic (\u201crest-and-digest\u201d) activity, slowing heart rate and breathing, easing muscle tension, and sometimes modestly lowering blood pressure. Regular practice may also lower stress-hormone levels, improve sleep, and alter brain activity involved in attention and emotional regulation, although effects vary by person and meditation technique.", "final": "Meditation can reduce sympathetic (\u201cfight-or-flight\u201d) activity and promote parasympathetic (\u201crest-and-digest\u201d) activity, slowing heart rate and breathing, easing muscle tension, and sometimes modestly lowering blood pressure. Regular practice may also lower stress-hormone levels, improve sleep, and alter brain activity involved in attention and emotional regulation, although effects vary by person and meditation technique."}
